WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Tabby. Your browser, with a little more focus. A real day in one minute.

00:03.000 --> 00:11.000
In Chrome's Tabby side panel, set the goal "Build a React login form" and start a 25-minute focus session.

00:11.000 --> 00:17.000
Tabby marks the real React state management documentation as On track and explains how it relates to the goal.

00:17.000 --> 00:24.000
A YouTube cat-video tab is marked Possible distraction. Tabby suggests returning to the saved work tab.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
The Back to work action returns Chrome to the React documentation.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
In Tasks, From page asks AI to create a task draft with a title and three steps.

00:34.000 --> 00:38.000
Review the draft and its source URL, then save the task.

00:38.000 --> 00:42.000
The saved task shows three steps and a link to the React documentation.

00:42.000 --> 00:49.000
In Tabs, ask for suggested groups and review React Documentation and Distractions before confirming.

00:49.000 --> 00:54.000
Chrome shows the newly created, named tab groups in its native tab strip.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
Return to the ongoing focus session. Tabby: less chaos, more focus. Built for the hackathon.
